{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_<scrubbed>","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016x68QSjhj3Qw1hiP6Rs83M","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Spec-context analysis for clarify Q1","subagent_type":"speckit-pro:spec-context-analyst","prompt":"You are being dispatched by speckit-autopilot's consensus dispatch logic to resolve a single unresolved clarify question. The question is tagged [spec], meaning it should be answered from the perspective of established project decisions, the constitution, and prior spec artifacts.\n\n## The question\n\nQ1: Should the new feature follow the project constitution's \"reversible writes\" principle, or is the constitution silent on this case?\n\nContext note from the clarify-executor: \"No external best-practice signal applies; this is purely a project-decision question.\"\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Locate and read the project constitution. Typical paths to check:\n   - `.specify/memory/constitution.md`\n   - `memory/constitution.md`\n   - `constitution.md` at repo root\n   - Any file under `.specify/` or `specs/` whose name contains \"constitution\"\n\n2. Search the constitution and prior spec artifacts for the term \"reversible writes\" (and related phrases: \"reversible\", \"rollback\", \"idempotent writes\", \"write safety\"). Use Grep with case-insensitive matching.\n\n3. If the constitution contains a \"reversible writes\" principle:\n   - Quote the exact text and cite file:line.\n   - Determine whether it applies to the new feature being clarified (read spec.md in the active feature directory under `specs/` to understand the feature scope).\n   - State whether the feature falls inside or outside the principle's stated scope.\n\n4. If the constitution does not contain a \"reversible writes\" principle:\n   - Confirm the absence with grep evidence (show the empty result).\n   - Check related principles (e.g., \"atomic operations\", \"idempotency\", \"data integrity\") that might be the intended reference.\n   - State clearly that the constitution is silent on this exact phrasing.\n\n5. Also check prior spec artifacts in `specs/` for any precedent — has a prior spec already adopted or rejected a \"reversible writes\" stance? Cite file:line if so.\n\n## Return format\n\nReturn a structured answer:\n- **Answer:** one of {yes, follow the principle | no, constitution is silent | partial — principle exists but scope unclear}\n- **Evidence:** file:line citations from the constitution and any related artifacts\n- **Confidence:** high | medium | low, with one sentence explaining why\n- **Recommendation for the synthesizer:** what the spec should say about reversible writes given the evidence\n\nKeep the response under 400 words. Do not write or edit any files — analysis only."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":"<scrubbed-usage>","diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<scrubbed-session>","uuid":"<scrubbed-uuid>"}
